WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.396
(happy music)

00:00:02.396 --> 00:00:04.394
- [Voiceover] This is Aiya and Shigu

00:00:04.394 --> 00:00:07.280
two adorable clouded leopard cubs.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.500
Don't be fooled by their youthful spirit.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.936
Clouded leopards are some of the most shy,

00:00:11.936 --> 00:00:14.689
mysterious and elusive cats.

00:00:14.689 --> 00:00:16.228
Besides their shy nature,

00:00:16.228 --> 00:00:18.921
they have a steadily declining population,

00:00:18.921 --> 00:00:22.605
making it even harder to
spot them in the wild.

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:27.132
As far as big cats go, clouded
leopards are the smallest.

00:00:27.132 --> 00:00:28.943
These two little girls will top out

00:00:28.943 --> 00:00:32.004
at around three feet when fully grown.

00:00:32.004 --> 00:00:35.700
Native throughout Asia, they
live in diverse habitats.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.715
From the rainforests of Indonesia

00:00:37.715 --> 00:00:40.971
to the foothills of the Himalayas.

00:00:40.971 --> 00:00:44.300
They pack a powerful bite
too, as they have the largest

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.098
canine teeth relative to
body size of any wild cat.

00:00:49.098 --> 00:00:51.693
They have short, powerful
legs and ankles that can

00:00:51.693 --> 00:00:55.443
rotate backwards, making
them elite climbers.

00:00:57.231 --> 00:00:59.522
Beyond a quickly shrinking habitat,

00:00:59.522 --> 00:01:02.918
poaching remains a huge
problem, as their skin,

00:01:02.918 --> 00:01:06.413
claws, teeth, bones and meat are all sold

00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:08.080
on the black market.

00:01:09.139 --> 00:01:11.472
This is the clouded leopard.

